WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.447
Step 1. Open a discussion list. Each encounter has its own discussions.

1.2
00:00:05.447 --> 00:00:10.120
Open the encounter from All Encounters, and select Notes.

2.1
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:14.679
Step 2. Read the discussion list. Each entry shows the title.

2.2
00:00:14.679 --> 00:00:20.124
The newest discussion is at the top, and there is no search or filter.

3.1
00:00:20.124 --> 00:00:23.481
Step 3. Open a discussion. Select its title.

3.2
00:00:23.481 --> 00:00:27.864
The heading shows the title and the number of messages.

4.1
00:00:27.864 --> 00:00:32.278
Step 4. Read the messages. The newest message is at the bottom.

4.2
00:00:32.278 --> 00:00:36.413
Point at the picture to see the username of the author.

5.1
00:00:36.413 --> 00:00:39.731
Step 5. Read the edit history of a message.

5.2
00:00:39.731 --> 00:00:46.226
Open Edit history under an edited message to see its earlier versions, newest first.

6.1
00:00:46.226 --> 00:00:49.344
Step 6. Keep the discussion up to date.

6.2
00:00:49.344 --> 00:00:52.728
Care checks for new messages every 30 seconds.

6.3
00:00:52.728 --> 00:00:56.170
To check now, select the refresh button.

7.1
00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:59.979
Step 7. Find the discussions of another encounter.

7.2
00:00:59.979 --> 00:01:03.608
Select Encounter History, then the other encounter.

7.3
00:01:03.608 --> 00:01:09.375
There you can only read; Care shows that you cannot send or edit messages.
